        {
          "id": "a",
          "text": "$(2x - 1)(x + 3)$"
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "text": "$(2x + 1)(x - 3)$"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "text": "$(2x + 3)(x - 1)$"
        },
        {
          "id": "d",
          "text": "$(2x - 3)(x + 1)$"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "b",
      "explanation": "$ac = 2 \\times (-3) = -6$. Two numbers that multiply to $-6$ and add to $-5$: $+1$ and $-6$. Split: $2x^2 + x - 6x - 3 = x(2x+1) - 3(2x+1) = (2x+1)(x-3)$."
    },
    {
      "id": "q7",
      "type": "multiple-choice",
      "difficulty": "knowledge-check",
      "stem": "Which expression is a factor of $4x^2 + 12x + 9$?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "text": "$(2x + 9)$"
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "text": "$(2x + 3)$"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "text": "$(4x + 3)$"
        },
        {
          "id": "d",
          "text": "$(x + 3)$"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "b",
      "explanation": "$4x^2 + 12x + 9 = (2x + 3)^2$. This is a perfect square since $4x^2 = (2x)^2$, $9 = 3^2$, and $12x = 2 \\times 2x \\times 3$."
    }
  ]
